      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Increasing lecithin can definitely introduce undesirable textural changes, potentially leading to a grittier mouthfeel or a slightly soapy flavor perceived by the consumer. While excessive surfactant addition can sometimes promote destabilization through micelle interference, the main risk at higher levels often relates to sensory perception and phase behavior rather than outright kinetic failure. It is best to optimize at the lowest effective concentration to maximize stability while preserving the intended sensory profile.",
      "source": "target",
